{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6 application screening fee cap","requirement":"A landlord may charge an application screening fee only if a rental unit is or will be available, and the fee may not exceed $30 per applicant, CPI-adjusted, or the actual out-of-pocket costs, whichever is less. The landlord must provide an itemized receipt and refund unused or unconsidered fees.","key_value":"$30 per applicant, CPI-adjusted annually since 1998-01-01","coverage_conditions":"Applies to any landlord of residential rental property who receives a request to rent from an applicant.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Federal or state housing assistance program rules on deposits and fees are not preempted.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"1998-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"In no case shall the amount of the application screening fee charged by the landlord or their agent be greater than thirty dollars ($30) per applicant. The thirty dollar ($30) application screening fee may be adjusted annually by the landlord or their agent commensurate with an increase in the Consumer Price Index, beginning on January 1, 1998.","interaction":"Does not preempt federal or state housing assistance program rules on deposits and fees.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6 application screening order","requirement":"A landlord must provide written screening criteria, consider completed applications in the order received, and approve the first applicant who meets the criteria. The landlord may not charge an application screening fee unless the application is actually considered.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies to any landlord of residential rental property who receives a request to rent from an applicant.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Federal or state housing assistance program rules on deposits and fees are not preempted.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"(i) Completed applications are considered, as provided for in the landlord’s established screening criteria, in the order in which the completed applications were received. The landlord’s screening criteria shall be provided to the applicant in writing together with the application form.\n(ii) The first applicant who meets the landlord’s established screening criteria is approved for tenancy.","interaction":"Does not preempt federal or state housing assistance program rules on deposits and fees.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
